  "description": "QORSEZ crystallizes in the cubic crystal system with space group I m -3 m. Reported CIF formula moiety: C66 H127 Ce4 N3 O35 Ti2. From the CIF bond table, Ce2 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce3 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce4 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce5 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce6 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce7 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ti1? (Ti) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 4.118-4.118 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 110.96-110.96°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [CeIV4TiIV2(O)4(OH)4(C(CH3)3COO)12]·3H2O·3MeCN. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
